) % m\n", "josephus_solver": "def solve(inputs: dict) -> float:\n    n = int(inputs['N'])\n    k = int(inputs['K'])\n    \n    # Josephus problem: find the survivor's position (0-indexed)\n    # Then convert to 1-indexed for the answer\n    \n    # Simulate the elimination process\n    people = list(range(1, n + 1))  # Positions 1 to n\n    current_index = 0\n    \n    while len(people) > 1:\n        # Count k people (including the current one)\n        # Move to the k-th person and eliminate them\n        current_index = (current_index + k - 1) % len(people)\n        people.pop(current_index)\n        # After removal, current_index is already at the next person\n        # (or wraps to 0 if we removed the last person)\n        if len(people) > 0:\n            current_index = current_index % len(people)\n    \n    return float(people[0])\n", "xorshift_solver": "def solve(inputs: dict) -> float:\n    x = int(inputs['X'])\n    a = int(inputs['A'])\n    b = int(inputs['B'])\n    c = int(inputs['C'])\n    k = int(inputs['K'])\n    \n    # Mask to keep within 32 bits\n    mask_32 = (1 << 32) - 1\n    \n    # Apply xorshift k times\n    for _ in range(k):\n        x = x ^ ((x << a) & mask_32)\n        x = x ^ ((x >> b) & mask_32)\n        x = x ^ ((x << c) & mask_32)\n        x = x & mask_32\n    \n    return float(x)\n"}, "transcript": [{"role": "user", "content": "PROBLEM 1 of 60:\nSolve the system of congruences: x is congruent to [709, 317, 1696, 62] modulo [1579, 557, 1979, 967] respectively (the moduli are pairwise coprime). Give the least non-negative x.\n\nThe named values in this problem are: {'REMAINDERS': [709, 317, 1696, 62], 'MODULI': [1579, 557, 1979, 967]} (keys: [REMAINDERS, MODULI]).\nGive your final answer to 12 significant figures, then call submit_answer with that number."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I need to solve a system of congruences using the Chinese Remainder Theorem (CRT). Let me write a script to handle this.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "t